</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendices</h2>

</section>
<section id="S1a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A.1 </span>Training Configurations</h2>

<div id="S1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we summarize the training configurations and hyperparameters used across the three stages of our framework: Driving Pre-training, Open-Loop Alignment, and Closed-Loop Alignment with HRL.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1.1 </span>Driving Pre-training</h3>

<div id="S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Driving pre-training includes the pre-training of the vision-language model (VLM), the end-to-end model (E2E), and the driving adapter.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">VLM Pre-Training.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use Qwen2.5VL-3B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> as our base model.
For each driving demonstration, we sample frames at 1 fps.
For every sampled frame, we obtain the corresponding decision label by applying the kinematic mapping function to the expert trajectories.
The detailed training configurations are listed in <a href="#S1.T1" title="In VLM Pre-Training. ‣ A.1.1 Driving Pre-training ‣ A.1 Training Configurations ‣ Senna-2: Aligning VLM and End-to-End Driving Policy for Consistent Decision Making and Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
