<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1.2 </span>Open-Loop Alignment</h3>

<div id="S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In each iteration, we first perform a two-step DDIM rollout to generate the predicted trajectory and compare it with the VLM decision.
Only the inconsistent samples are used for training.
The loss weight <math id="S1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 1.
During optimization, we apply LoRA finetuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> to the VLM while fully finetuning the remaining modules.
The detailed hyperparameters are listed in <a href="#S1.T4" title="In A.1.2 Open-Loop Alignment ‣ A.1 Training Configurations ‣ Senna-2: Aligning VLM and End-to-End Driving Policy for Consistent Decision Making and Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
