<td id="S1.T5.7.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">optimizer hyper-parameters</span></td>
<td id="S1.T5.7.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><math id="S1.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2},\epsilon=0.9,0.999,1\times 10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0.9</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0.999</mn><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn mathsize="0.800em">10</mn><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2},\epsilon=0.9,0.999,1\times 10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T5.7.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T5.7.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">weight decay</span></td>
<td id="S1.T5.7.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T5.7.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T5.7.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">batch size</span></td>
<td id="S1.T5.7.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">128</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T5.7.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T5.7.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">training steps</span></td>
<td id="S1.T5.7.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">500</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T5.7.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T5.7.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">LoRA hyperparameters</span></td>
<td id="S1.T5.7.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><math id="S1.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,\alpha=8,16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">8</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,\alpha=8,16</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T5.7.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T5.7.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.10.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">training GPU</span></td>
<td id="S1.T5.7.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="S1.T5.7.10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">64 NVIDIA L20</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A.2 </span>Kinematic Mapping Function</h2>

<div id="S2a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce the implementation details on the kinematic mapping function <math id="S2a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{k}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{k}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This function is used to convert trajectories into high-level decision labels for two purposes:
generating ground-truth decisions from expert data, and inferring decisions from E2E planning for consistency checking with VLM outputs.
We describe the function in two parts: speed and direction control.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2a.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For speed control, given a trajectory, we first extract the first 1.5s subsequence <math id="S2a.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\left\{\tau_{t}\right\}^{14}_{t=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>14</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\left\{\tau_{t}\right\}^{14}_{t=0}</annotation></semantics></math> with a timestep of <math id="S2a.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>s. The speed <math id="S2a.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and acceleration <math id="S2a.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed as</p>
<table id="S2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=\frac{\lVert\tau_{t}-\tau_{t-1}\rVert}{\Delta t},\quad a_{t}=\frac{v_{t}-v_{t-1}}{\Delta t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=\frac{\lVert\tau_{t}-\tau_{t-1}\rVert}{\Delta t},\quad a_{t}=\frac{v_{t}-v_{t-1}}{\Delta t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2a.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and smooth both with an average filter of window size <math id="S2a.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=5</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S2a.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{lcs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>lcs</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{lcs}}</annotation></semantics></math> return the length of the longest continuous True segment in a Boolean sequence, and <math id="S2a.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMS}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>RMS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMS}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> return the mean square sum.
Then the trajectory is labeled as <span id="S2a.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">accelerate</span> if</p>
<table id="S2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}a_{1}&gt;0,\quad f_{\text{lcs}}(a_{t}&gt;0.3)\geq 8,\\
\max(a_{t})&gt;0.6,\quad\text{RMS}(a_{t})&gt;0.4.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>lcs</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>RMS</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}a_{1}&gt;0,\quad f_{\text{lcs}}(a_{t}&gt;0.3)\geq 8,\\
\max(a_{t})&gt;0.6,\quad\text{RMS}(a_{t})&gt;0.4.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2a.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The trajectory is labeled as <span id="S2a.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">decelerate</span> if</p>
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}a_{1}&lt;0,\quad f_{\text{lcs}}(a_{t}&lt;-0.3)\geq 8,\\
\min(a_{t})&lt;-0.6,\quad\text{RMS}(a_{t})&gt;0.4.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>lcs</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>RMS</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}a_{1}&lt;0,\quad f_{\text{lcs}}(a_{t}&lt;-0.3)\geq 8,\\
\min(a_{t})&lt;-0.6,\quad\text{RMS}(a_{t})&gt;0.4.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2a.p2.4" class="ltx_p">If neither condition is met, we compute the average speed <math id="S2a.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and acceleration <math id="S2a.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The label is assigned as <span id="S2a.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">keep speed</span> if</p>
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}|\bar{a}|&lt;0.3\cdot s_{a},\\
\max(|a_{t}|)&lt;0.6\cdot s_{a},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}|\bar{a}|&lt;0.3\cdot s_{a},\\
\max(|a_{t}|)&lt;0.6\cdot s_{a},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2a.p2.5" class="ltx_p">or <span id="S2a.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">stop</span> if <math id="S2a.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="S2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{a}=\begin{cases}2.5,&amp;\bar{v}&gt;25,\\
2,&amp;20&lt;\bar{v}\leq 25,\\
1.5,&amp;10&lt;\bar{v}\leq 20,\\
1.25,&amp;5&lt;\bar{v}\leq 10,\\
1,&amp;otherwise.\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{a}=\begin{cases}2.5,&amp;\bar{v}&gt;25,\\
2,&amp;20&lt;\bar{v}\leq 25,\\
1.5,&amp;10&lt;\bar{v}\leq 20,\\
1.25,&amp;5&lt;\bar{v}\leq 10,\\
1,&amp;otherwise.\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2a.p2.6" class="ltx_p">If none of the above conditions hold, the speed label is considered unknown and ignored.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2a.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2a.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For direction control, we consider two cases.
For the predicted trajectory, we first compute the average speed <math id="S2a.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum and minimum lateral displacement <math id="S2a.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta y_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta y_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2a.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta y_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta y_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the maximum yaw variation <math id="S2a.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\psi_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\psi_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> within the 1.5-second horizon, relative to the initial time.
The direction decision label <math id="S2a.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{kmf}}_{\text{dir}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>dir</mtext><mtext>kmf</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{kmf}}_{\text{dir}}</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned as</p>
<table id="S2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{kmf}}_{\text{dir}}=\begin{cases}\text{{left}},&amp;\text{if }\Delta\psi_{\text{max}}&gt;s_{\psi}\text{ and }\Delta y_{\text{max}}&gt;s_{y},\\
\text{{right}},&amp;\text{if }\Delta\psi_{\text{max}}&gt;s_{\psi}\text{ and }\Delta y_{\text{min}}&lt;-s_{y},\\
\text{{staight}},&amp;otherwise,\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>dir</mtext><mtext>kmf</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">left</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">right</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">staight</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{kmf}}_{\text{dir}}=\begin{cases}\text{{left}},&amp;\text{if }\Delta\psi_{\text{max}}&gt;s_{\psi}\text{ and }\Delta y_{\text{max}}&gt;s_{y},\\
\text{{right}},&amp;\text{if }\Delta\psi_{\text{max}}&gt;s_{\psi}\text{ and }\Delta y_{\text{min}}&lt;-s_{y},\\
\text{{staight}},&amp;otherwise,\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2a.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2a.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\psi}=\frac{\pi}{36}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\psi}=\frac{\pi}{36}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="S2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{y}=\begin{cases}3,&amp;\bar{v}&gt;15,\\
2.4,&amp;10&lt;\bar{v}\leq 15,\\
1.5,&amp;5&lt;\bar{v}\leq 10,\\
0.9,&amp;3&lt;\bar{v}\leq 5,\\
0.45,&amp;otherwise.\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2.4</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.45</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{y}=\begin{cases}3,&amp;\bar{v}&gt;15,\\
2.4,&amp;10&lt;\bar{v}\leq 15,\\
1.5,&amp;5&lt;\bar{v}\leq 10,\\
0.9,&amp;3&lt;\bar{v}\leq 5,\\
0.45,&amp;otherwise.\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2a.p3.3" class="ltx_p">For VLM pre-training, we employ frame-level expert annotations <math id="S2a.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{gt}}_{\text{dir}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>dir</mtext><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{gt}}_{\text{dir}}</annotation></semantics></math> as ground truth. These annotations encompass multiple categories, including <span id="S2a.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">go straight</span>, <span id="S2a.p3.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">turn left</span>, <span id="S2a.p3.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">turn right</span>, <span id="S2a.p3.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">change lane left</span>, and <span id="S2a.p3.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">change lane right</span>.
During consistency checking, the fine-grained VLM decisions are projected onto the coarse decision classes used by the E2E policy as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{vlm}}_{\text{dir}}=\begin{cases}\text{{left}},&amp;\text{if }d^{\text{gt}}_{\text{dir}}\in\left\{\text{{turn left}, {change lane left}}\right\},\\
\text{{right}},&amp;\text{if }d^{\text{gt}}_{\text{dir}}\in\left\{\text{{turn right}, {change lane right}}\right\},\\
\text{{staight}},&amp;otherwise.\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>dir</mtext><mtext>vlm</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">left</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>dir</mtext><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">turn left</mtext><mtext>, </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">change lane left</mtext></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">right</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>dir</mtext><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">turn right</mtext><mtext>, </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">change lane right</mtext></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">staight</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{vlm}}_{\text{dir}}=\begin{cases}\text{{left}},&amp;\text{if }d^{\text{gt}}_{\text{dir}}\in\left\{\text{{turn left}, {change lane left}}\right\},\\
\text{{right}},&amp;\text{if }d^{\text{gt}}_{\text{dir}}\in\left\{\text{{turn right}, {change lane right}}\right\},\\
\text{{staight}},&amp;otherwise.\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.11219v1/dynamics.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/352;" width="685" height="352" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A1</span>: </span><span id="S2.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Learning curve across the whole training pipeline.<span id="S2.F1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (a) Driving pretraining. (b) Open-loop alignment. (c) Closed-loop alignment with HRL. The dashed line denotes the performance of the extended driving-pretraining baseline.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.F2a" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.11219v1/extend_vis0__.png" id="S2.F2a.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:685/571;" width="685" height="571" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2a.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A2</span>: </span><span id="S2.F2a.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">More qualitative results in the cut-in scenarios.<span id="S2.F2a.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In these cases, Senna <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> often reacts too late and leads to near-collision outcomes, while our policy maintains coherent decision–planning coupling and ensures safe avoidance.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A.3 </span>Training Dynamics</h2>

<div id="S3a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As illustrated in <a href="#S2.F1" title="In A.2 Kinematic Mapping Function ‣ Senna-2: Aligning VLM and End-to-End Driving Policy for Consistent Decision Making and Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A1</span></a>, the learning curves highlight the effectiveness of our three-stage pipeline.
Driving pretraining enables the model to acquire core driving competencies from large-scale demonstrations efficiently.
Open-loop alignment substantially enhances decision–planning consistency, delivering greater performance gains than simply prolonging pretraining.
Finally, closed-loop alignment with HRL requires only limited additional training yet produces marked improvements in interactive driving performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A.4 </span>More Qualitative Results</h2>

<div id="S4a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present additional visualizations in <a href="#S2.F2a" title="In A.2 Kinematic Mapping Function ‣ Senna-2: Aligning VLM and End-to-End Driving Policy for Consistent Decision Making and Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.F3" title="In A.4 More Qualitative Results ‣ Senna-2: Aligning VLM and End-to-End Driving Policy for Consistent Decision Making and Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A3</span></a> that compare our method against the baseline <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> across a wide range of scenarios, including cut-in, right-turn, lane-change, and hard-braking events.
These qualitative results highlight the performance gains and improved consistency achieved by our approach under diverse driving conditions, particularly in high-risk interactions where the baseline often reacts late or produces inconsistent planning, leading to near-collision behaviors.
Corresponding video visualizations are included in the supplementary material for clearer dynamic interpretation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.11219v1/extend_vis1__.png" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:685/769;" width="685" height="769" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A3</span>: </span><span id="S4.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">More qualitative results in diverse scenarios.<span id="S4.F3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
(a) Our policy safely handles a hard-braking event, while the baseline causes a collision.
(b) During a right turn, our method avoids the cyclist, whereas the baseline crashes.
(c) Our policy completes the lane change, but the baseline drifts across lanes.
(d) Our method aborts the lane change upon hazard detection, while the baseline is rear-ended.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
</div>
